34,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It turns out the morning routine upstairs takes a while—between four and nine minutes just to get set up! Also, people arrive at totally different times, some way before eight and others after ten.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The floor billing is based on area, not headcount, meaning we pay for empty desks. Also, re-running power and network costs 6,200 yen per desk every single time we change the layout.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The staff survey shows that daylight is a major complaint, yet the current plan leaves three people against the interior wall. Also, the new joiners learned a lot just by overhearing us.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The sound levels are significantly higher by the printer and door, and the physio noted that it takes days of small adjustments to get a workstation's ergonomics actually right.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found out that unplanned shuffles in the past year caused weeks of interruptions! But on the bright side, when project strands sat together last spring, we barely needed written notes because we just talked.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if people arrive at such different times, a first-come-first-served system would be totally unfair! The early birds would always get the best spots.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Exactly. And given the cost of re-running power and network for every change, we cannot afford a system that requires frequent physical adjustments or constant shuffling.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"That's a good point, Toshio. But we also can't ignore that the current plan leaves some people in the dark, and the joiners' experience shows that proximity really helps with learning.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"If it takes days to settle into a workstation's ergonomics, any system that forces us to move frequently is a nightmare for our physical health.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,And the shuffle history proves that moving around is a huge distraction! But the project strand data shows that sitting together is a huge win for our communication.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"So, if we move every day or every few weeks, we're wasting time in the morning and hurting our backs! We need something that doesn't make us scramble.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The financial data suggests we should avoid any plan that requires frequent re-wiring or paying for unused space. A permanent, stable layout seems the most fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"But a permanent layout might just cement the unfairness of who gets the window and who doesn't. We need a way to ensure the ""dark"" spots aren't just handed to the same people forever.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"I agree with Mizuki. If we go with fixed desks, we have to be very careful about who is placed in those high-noise areas or the dark spots, because we can't just move easily.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"But if we don't have fixed spots, we lose that magic of just overhearing things and chatting! We need a balance between stability and the social benefits of sitting together.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm starting to think that any system where we have to plug in and set up every single morning is just too much of a hassle.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Between the setup time Rin found and the wiring costs I discovered, a free-address system is both inefficient and expensive. We need a more stable arrangement.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want to avoid the unfairness of fixed spots while keeping the stability Toshio wants, maybe we should consider something that rotates, so everyone eventually gets a window.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Rotating blocks might solve the window issue, but if the physio is right, we'd be spending a huge chunk of our year just trying to get our chairs and monitors comfortable again.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"That's a fair point, Shion. But if we just stay in one spot forever, we might miss out on the chance to bond with different teammates! We have to weigh the physical comfort against the team's energy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
