60,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I'm leaning toward Fixed Desks by Function. It stops the morning scramble and the unfairness of who arrives first, and it seems the most stable for everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Fixed Desks by Function is the only option that minimizes recurring wiring costs and avoids the waste of time and money associated with constant movement.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I'm torn, but I think Fixed Desks by Function is the safest bet if we explicitly decide how to distribute the window seats and noise levels fairly.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"I'm still worried about the ergonomics, but Rotating Blocks would be a physical nightmare. Fixed Desks by Function is the only way to actually settle into a workstation and stay comfortable.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I'm worried we'll lose that spontaneous communication, but the shuffle interruptions were too much. I'll vote for Fixed Desks by Function so we can at least group the right people together!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,It seems like we've all reached the same conclusion! It's the only way to make sure the morning doesn't turn into a race for the best desk.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"It is the most logical choice. By eliminating the costs of frequent re-wiring and the inefficiency of daily setup, we protect both our budget and our time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"As long as we are honest about the window seats and the noise, I'm on board. Let's make sure the assignment process is transparent.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"I'm satisfied. If we commit to fixed desks, we can finally set our equipment once and not have to deal with the physical strain of constant readjustment.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I'm happy as long as we use the ""function"" part to keep the people who need to collaborate close together! Let's do it!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm ready to vote! I'll go with Option C: Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I vote for Option C: Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for Option C: Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,I vote for Option C: Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I vote for Option C: Fixed Desks by Function!,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
